PURPOSE

DG-1R-05Q through DG-1R-05AB established positive component results for:

- independently qualified first-shot repair;
- phenotype-health refresh;
- within-role adaptation;
- distributed role migration;
- provenance-lineage qualification;
- append-only causal history;
- lineage-qualified registry quorum;
- cross-layer sovereignty composition;
- partition / causal re-merge;
- ancestry-linked hereditary capsules;
- hibernation / reactivation with expired dormant authority.

Those mechanisms have now been tested individually and in partial compositions.

DG-1R-05AC asks the pre-application question:

CAN THE CLOSED MECHANISMS
COEXIST ACROSS ONE PERSISTENT SYNTHETIC DEVELOPMENTAL LIFECYCLE
WITHOUT HIDDEN CENTRAL OPERATIONAL AUTHORITY,
CROSS-LAYER AUTHORITY LEAKS,
STALE IDENTITY NORMALIZATION,
OR CONTRADICTORY HISTORICAL ANCHORS?

05AC is a composition audit.

It does not search for a better local threshold.
It does not retune a closed component.

BOUNDARY

Synthetic software only.

No living tissue.
No wetware.
No biological nanotechnology.
No production mutation.
No CKB / KTRADE integration.
No canonical DG-1R-05 execution.
No STAB-18-R1 execution.

NON-CANONICAL.

DG-1R-05 canonical frozen primary remains UNSPENT.

FROZEN COMPONENT CONTRACTS

05AC consumes the following closed semantics without changing their thresholds.

05Q — REPAIR AUTHORITY

Qualified true damage may authorize one bounded first-shot repair.
Check-only / ambiguous evidence abstains.
Repair authority is not granted by raw syndrome descent alone.

05R — PHENOTYPE-HEALTH COMMIT

A stable cell may refresh phenotype-health memory only after:
- current structural consistency;
- independent peer confirmation of functional identity;
- no unresolved damage.

Stable corruption alone is insufficient.

05S / 05W — ROLE / REGISTRY AUTHORITY

Role migration requires four lineage-qualified governance classes:
DEMAND_A
DEMAND_B
PEER_A
PEER_B.

Registry event / seal authority requires three pairwise-disjoint verified provenance roots.

Holder count is not evidence count.

05X — CROSS-LAYER ORDERING

Frozen order:

1. resolve damage / quarantine first;
2. do not advance health identity across unresolved damage;
3. old role remains authoritative until full role transaction commits;
4. new lineage cannot vote before verification;
5. stale generation cannot overwrite newer authority;
6. lower-layer abstention propagates upward;
7. failed composed transactions preserve the last fully committed authority.

05Y — PARTITION / RE-MERGE

Partition-local actions are provisional.

At re-merge:
- disjoint-target changes commute;
- identical concurrent outcomes coalesce;
- same-target conflicting role changes roll back to the last common committed state;
- population size never breaks causal conflict ties;
- stale histories cannot overwrite newer verified descendants.

05AB — HEREDITARY TEMPORAL MEMORY

Exact five-field hereditary capsule:

checkpoint_id;
generation;
role;
fp2;
causal_cursor.

No extra field is added.

A capsule becomes authoritative only after full relevant ancestry verification:
- genesis continuity;
- contiguous generation sequence;
- recomputed parent-linked commit IDs;
- older qualified sealed checkpoints;
- selected anchor;
- terminal current state.

05AA — HIBERNATION / REACTIVATION

Dormant cells preserve identity but carry zero current authority.

Reactivation stages remain:

R0_WAKE_PASSIVE
R1_CAUSAL_CATCHUP
R2_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION
R3_HEALTH_DWELL
R4_AUTHORITY_RESTORATION

A former witness slot is not reclaimed automatically.
Fresh current registration is required.

PERSISTENT ORGANISM FIXTURE

12 cells.

Initial ROLE(cell) = cell mod 4.

Each cell carries:

- current role;
- FP2 phenotype;
- role generation;
- health generation;
- active / dormant / quarantined state;
- causal cursor;
- current holder assignments if any.

Organism carries distributed records for:

- role-governance events;
- registry edges and seals;
- lineage roots;
- temporal capsules;
- partition-provisional events.

The harness may centrally simulate the world for reproducibility.

That simulator is evaluator infrastructure only.

No synthetic cell receives an omniscient operational oracle.

DEVELOPMENTAL EPOCHS

One lifecycle consists of 16 sealed epochs.

Frozen sequence:

E0  GENESIS
E1  CLEAN OPERATION
E2  TRUE DAMAGE
E3  QUALIFIED REPAIR
E4  HEALTH-MEMORY COMMIT
E5  WITHIN-ROLE ADAPTATION
E6  ROLE-MIGRATION PROPOSAL
E7  ROLE-MIGRATION COMMIT
E8  HEREDITARY CAPSULE SEAL
E9  TARGET HIBERNATION
E10 LIVE-POPULATION WITNESS ROTATION
E11 LEGITIMATE ROLE CHANGE WHILE TARGET SLEEPS
E12 TARGET REACTIVATION / CAUSAL CATCH-UP
E13 COMMUNICATION PARTITION
E14 PARTITION-LOCAL PROVISIONAL EVENTS
E15 RE-MERGE / FINAL SEAL

The exact target cell rotates across cases.

No stage may be skipped merely because a later stage would make the final state convenient.

PRIMARY AUDITS

AUDIT A — CLEAN 16-EPOCH LIFECYCLE

For every target cell:

run the full 16-epoch sequence with no adversarial corruption.

Required:

- final state sealed;
- zero stale authority;
- zero unresolved quarantine;
- final target role / FP2 internally consistent;
- hereditary capsule remains a valid ancestor;
- dormant authority count zero during E9-E11;
- reactivated authority restored only after E12 catch-up.

Cases:

12.

AUDIT B — DAMAGE -> REPAIR -> HEALTH COMMIT ORDER

For every cell and each true-damage family:

TRUE_SINGLE
TRUE_TWO_PLANE
TRUE_COORDINATED

36 cases.

Required:

- health generation cannot advance at E2;
- bounded repair completes at E3;
- health generation may advance only at E4;
- repaired state is not treated as pre-damage historical identity;
- no false role change is induced.

AUDIT C — CHECK-ONLY / AMBIGUOUS DAMAGE

For every cell:

inject a check-only integrity disturbance at E2.

12 cases.

Required:

- repair abstains;
- no logical state flip;
- health commit does not normalize an unresolved ambiguity;
- later role migration is blocked until ambiguity is resolved or explicitly cleared by the frozen rule.

AUDIT D — WITHIN-ROLE ADAPTATION

For every cell:

apply a role-preserving internal adaptation at E5.

12 cases.

Required:

- current role unchanged;
- FP2 phenotype equivalence preserved;
- no spurious role migration;
- capsule ancestry remains valid.

AUDIT E — ROLE MIGRATION ATOMICITY

For every target cell and each alternate role:

36 cases.

Required:

- proposal alone does not change authority;
- complete four-class qualified commit changes role exactly once;
- role generation increments exactly once;
- FP2 becomes the new ROLE2-equivalent phenotype;
- partial governance evidence abstains.

AUDIT F — HIBERNATION ACROSS LIVE ROLE CHANGE

For every target cell and each alternate role:

36 cases.

Target sleeps at E9.
Live population commits a legitimate newer target role at E11.

Required:

- dormant target casts zero votes;
- wake does not restore old role;
- full ancestry catch-up succeeds;
- current newer role is accepted;
- authority restores only after health dwell / current registration.

AUDIT G — WITNESS HIBERNATION / REPLACEMENT

For each of the four governance slots
and each of 12 target cells:

48 cases.

Required:

- sleeping holder contributes zero current votes;
- replacement receives fresh lineage generation;
- effective independent class count remains unchanged;
- waking old holder does not automatically reclaim the slot.

AUDIT H — TEMPORAL SENTINEL CONTINUITY DURING LIFECYCLE

For every target cell:

seal a five-field capsule at E8.

After later legitimate role change and hibernation:

Required:
- full ancestry verification succeeds;
- old-role mismatch does not veto legitimate development;
- rewriting an earlier sealed checkpoint contests the history;
- same capsule fields remain sufficient.

12 clean + 12 rewrite challenges.

AUDIT I — PARTITION WITH DISJOINT TARGET CHANGES

For every A-side target paired with every B-side target:

6 x 6 = 36 cases.

At E13 split cells 0..5 from 6..11.

Each side commits one qualified provisional change to a different target.

Required:

- both survive re-merge;
- final result independent of merge input order;
- pre-partition provenance is not double-counted.

AUDIT J — PARTITION SAME-TARGET ROLE CONFLICT

For every target cell
and every ordered pair of distinct alternate roles:

12 x 6 = 72 cases.

Required:

- neither conflicting branch becomes final solely by population size;
- target rolls back to last common committed role;
- unrelated targets remain mergeable;
- fresh post-merge decision required.

AUDIT K — STALE DORMANT SNAPSHOT PLUS REPAIR

For every target cell:

sleep from a healthy state,
advance live role,
corrupt dormant local state,
wake.

12 cases.

Required:

- stale snapshot cannot overwrite newer role;
- corrupted dormant local state quarantines;
- repair reconciles to current authoritative phenotype;
- old health generation does not overwrite current health memory.

AUDIT L — SAME-LINEAGE FANOUT ACROSS LAYERS

For nominal holder counts:

4, 8, 16, 32, 64

repeat one root lineage into:
- governance witnesses;
- registry replicas;
- dormant sentinels.

15 cases total.

Required:

- no layer converts copied holder count into independent provenance;
- no false role commit;
- no false registry seal;
- no false temporal quorum.

AUDIT M — INCOMPLETE CAUSAL HISTORY DURING REACTIVATION

For every cell and omitted epoch position:

first;
middle;
last-precurrent.

36 cases.

Required:

- reactivation remains nonauthoritative;
- hereditary continuity does not validate;
- no fresh vote registration;
- last fully committed global state preserved.

AUDIT N — PARTIAL FINAL WRITES / CROSS-LAYER ROLLBACK

For each transactional layer:

REPAIR_RECEIPT
HEALTH_COMMIT
ROLE_COMMIT
REGISTRY_SEAL
REACTIVATION_REGISTRATION
PARTITION_MERGE

and each cut point:

BEFORE_FIRST_WRITE
AFTER_FIRST_WRITE
BEFORE_FINAL_CERTIFICATE

18 cases.

Required:

- incomplete transaction never becomes authoritative;
- rollback / abstention leaves last complete authority intact;
- no dangling provisional authority.

AUDIT O — REPEATED DEVELOPMENTAL LIFECYCLES

For every cell:

run four complete lifecycle rounds.

48 cell-lifecycles.

Required:

- causal cursor monotonic;
- role generation monotonic;
- health generation monotonic;
- no stale vote;
- no duplicated authority;
- all temporal capsules remain either valid ancestors or explicitly superseded by later sealed capsules;
- final history has one authoritative head.

AUDIT P — LOCAL-ONLY ORDERING NEGATIVE CONTROL

Remove only the cross-layer ordering constraints while leaving local component rules unchanged.

Required exposure:

at least one of:
- damaged state can be health-committed;
- stale role can regain authority;
- unverified lineage can vote;
- partial role / registry state leaks authority.

Signal:

CROSS_LAYER_ORDERING_NECESSARY.

